From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Read EDID segments from the EDID address

An E-DDC read of EDID blocks 2 and up starts with the segment pointer
message to 0x30. The I2C master takes the slave address from the first
message, so the data was read from 0x30 and the blocks came back as
zeroes. Use the EDID address 0x50 then, as dw-hdmi-qp does.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
index 8546100..e4d4939 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -459,7 +459,14 @@ static int dw_hdmi_i2c_xfer(struct i2c_adapter *adap,
 	/* Unmute DONE and ERROR interrupts */
 	hdmi_writeb(hdmi, 0x00, HDMI_IH_MUTE_I2CM_STAT0);
 
-	/* Set slave device address taken from the first I2C message */
+	/*
+	 * Set slave device address taken from the first I2C message. An
+	 * E-DDC read starts with the segment pointer write to 0x30; the
+	 * data itself comes from the EDID address.
+	 */
+	if (addr == DDC_SEGMENT_ADDR && msgs[0].len == 1)
+		addr = DDC_ADDR;
+
 	hdmi_writeb(hdmi, addr, HDMI_I2CM_SLAVE);
 
 	/* Set slave device register address on transfer */
-- 
